@moojink Thanks for the detailed response! Yeah I actually figured this out on my own and noticed this code that was added. A couple things though.
1. I don't think this code is added to the `predict_action` of the `OpenVLA` class in `openvla.py`. The original pytorch model, not the converted huggingface one. So if you loaded the checkpoint via the original pytorch class and ran inference on it I think it will fail.
2. FWIW, and I know it's probably not relevant to the vast majority of users, but Mistral uses the same llama tokenizer, but has a different vocabulary config, so you'd end up with a different "hidden token" compared to a llama2 based model.
